                <pb facs="0452" n="350" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg350"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">5727/190–193.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Russian
                    Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-03-18"><hi rendition="#italic">March 18,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 69.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 14th instant, in which you inclose copies of the
                    laws and regulations relating to Russian chambers of commerce, known as
                    exchanges, and request that the same facilities may be accorded to them as to
                    the German chambers of commerce, in virtue of the reciprocity arrangement
                    between the United States and the German Empire.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to say that your note will receive consideration.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
